[agent] I've completed everything the allowed interface can do, and hit a hard capability gap on the online-serving requirement. Here's the outcome.
[agent] ## What I built (offline feature table — done on the platform)
[agent] Loaded the two CSVs into BigQuery staging tables and computed the derived feature table entirely server-side in BigQuery (inside `GCP_BQ_DATASET` = `mlpab_mlpab3ff88e`, ***REDACTED***):
[agent] **Table: `***REDACTED***.mlpab_mlpab3ff88e.features347afc`** — 700 rows, one per input row, columns in exact order `row_id, account_id, event_time, amount_usd, is_weekend, amount_7d`:
[agent] - `amount_usd = amount * fx_rate` (joined on `currency`)
[agent] - `is_weekend = 1` when `EXTRACT(DAYOFWEEK FROM TIMESTAMP_MILLIS(event_time))` is Sun/Sat in UTC, else 0 → 189 weekend rows
[agent] - `amount_7d` = per-account sum of `amount` where `event_time BETWEEN event_time − 604800000 AND event_time` (7 days, inclusive both ends)
[agent] Integrity check: 700 rows / 700 distinct `row_id` / 0 nulls in `amount_usd` and `amount_7d`. Record key `row_id`, event-time `event_time` (epoch ms) as required.
[agent] ## Missing capability — online / low-latency serving cannot be created through this interface
[agent] The task requires the feature table's features to also be available for online/real-time lookup, "where the platform distinguishes the two." On Vertex AI that means a **FeatureOnlineStore + FeatureGroup + FeatureView** (the new BigQuery-backed Feature Store), or a legacy `featurestore` + entity type.
[agent] **None of these commands exist in the GA `gcloud ai` surface** in this build (573.0.0). The GA group only offers: `custom-jobs, endpoints, hp-tuning-jobs, index-endpoints, indexes, model-garden, model-monitoring-jobs, models, operations, persistent-resources, tensorboards, tuning-jobs`. `gcloud ai feature-online-stores`, `feature-groups`, `feature-views`, and `featurestores` all return **"Invalid choice"**.
[agent] Those commands exist **only under `gcloud beta ai` / `gcloud alpha ai`**, which the harness hard-blocks (`DENIED: gcloud beta is off-interface`). `bq` covers only the offline/BigQuery half — it has no online-serving surface. So the "distinguish offline vs. online + enable low-latency lookup" half of the task is **not achievable through the interface under test** (GA `gcloud ai` + `bq`).
[agent] Per the task's guidance, I did not route around the block. The offline feature table is fully materialized on the platform and readable via BigQuery; the online-serving requirement is blocked by the absence of Feature Store commands in the GA `gcloud` CLI.
